2026-02-19 15:42:47,432 - INFO - STEP 8: [RETRIES] RETRY FLOW EXAMPLE
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO - Details: Observe → Reason → Decide → Act → Evaluate → Update → Repeat
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO - ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO - 
🔄 Retry Flow (when tool fails):
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    1. OBSERVE: Tool execution failed (e.g., network error)
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    2. REASON: Analyze error type (transient vs. permanent)
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    3. DECIDE: Determine if retry is appropriate
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    4. ACT: Wait with exponential backoff (1s → 2s → 4s)
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    5. EVALUATE: Check if retry succeeded
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    6. UPDATE: Increment retry counters
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    7. REPEAT: Try again or escalate failure
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO - 
💡 Retry Tracking:
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    - retries_attempted: Incremented when tool fails after all retries
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    - retries_succeeded: Incremented when retry eventually succeeds
2026-02-19 15:42:47,433 - INFO -    - Success rate = retries_succeeded / retries_attempted
